          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: Recent testimony of an old observation: A witness observes in April 2006 at 10 a.m. (the exact date is not specified, a arbitrary date is given here) the silent and straight movement of a black object in the sky. The speed is constant and the object disappears on the horizon. The witness compares the object to a \"barrel of oil\" or a \"black cabin.\" The relatively low altitude, the black barrel-shaped object, the slow movement that might be with the wind, suggest a thermal (solar) balloon. Since the date is unknown, this hypothesis cannot be confirmed. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"C\": lack of information.",
